  "known_local_policies": [
    "Both Secrets redirect the same accepted opponent attack window. Declaration, forced flag, opportunity consumption and original hero weapon wear identity remain unchanged.",
    "Misdirection samples each other live physical character once across both players, excluding the attacker and currently protected hero. Friendly heroes, friendly minions and opposing minions are possible. Replacement does not rerun voluntary taunt/stealth/immune targeting; protection still applies during combat.",
    "Sudden Betrayal samples only immediate physical left/right slots of the attacking minion. Dormant/noncharacter slots block rather than bridge; inactive, mortally wounded or doomed neighbors are excluded. Exact current CN immunity eligibility and secret reaction order remain uncalibrated local policies.",
    "No candidate keeps an unrevealed Secret and consumes no RNG. A revealed Secret whose actual domain disappears has no redirect and no RNG. A sole candidate uses no RNG; multiple candidates use one ordinary uniform random choice with complete MT19937 receipts.",
    "Historical2019/2020 first-person weapon reports support active-turn hero weapon retaliation after Misdirection without defender weapon wear. Physical adjacency and RNG policy remain local until independent CN calibration.",
    "An already accepted native attack substitution retains its captured member plan and target. It is not rewritten by a later original-window redirect; exact 2022 Neptulon report and current CN order remain recorded boundaries."
  ]
